{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בחמר", :translit "b'chomer", :gloss "in mortar"} {:he "ברמ\"ח איברים", :translit "b'rimach eivarim", :gloss "248 limbs"} {:he "ד' מיני ענויין", :translit "da' minei inuiyin", :gloss "four types of affliction"} {:he "וימררו את חייהם בעבודה קשה בחמר ובלבנים ובכל עבודה בשדה את כל עבודתם אשר עבדו בהם בפרך", :translit "va'yemareru et chayeihem ba'avodah kashah b'chomer uvil'vanim uchol avodah basadeh et kol avodatam asher avdu bahem b'farekh", :gloss "And they embittered their lives with hard labor with mortar and with bricks and with all labor in the field all their labor which they worked upon them with rigor"} {:he "ד' מכות", :translit "da' makot", :gloss "four plagues"} {:he "ה' מכות", :translit "hei makot", :gloss "five plagues"} {:he "ויעבידו מצרים את בני ישראל בפרך", :translit "va'ya'avidu mitzrayim et b'nei yisra'el b'farekh", :gloss "And the Egyptians worked the Children of Israel with rigor"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "בחמר", :b "רמ״ח איברים"}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah counts 248 limbs in the human body (Mishnah Oholot 1:8). Rabban Gamliel lists ten plagues that struck the Egyptians in Egypt (Mishnah Makkot 3:16; Mishnah Eduyot 2:10), while a baraita enumerates that the Egyptians were struck by ten plagues at the sea, derived from the finger of God versus the hand of God (Shabbat 88a does not address this; the source for the division of plagues into groups corresponding to the afflictions appears in midrashic collections that link the number of plagues to the number of servitude categories). The phrase 'בפרך' is interpreted by the Sages to mean 'with a soft mouth' — that Pharaoh deceived them into volunteer labor before imposing it by force (Sotah 11b).", :sources ["Mishnah Oholot 1:8" "Mishnah Makkot 3:16" "Mishnah Eduyot 2:10" "Sotah 11b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "בחמר", :a-value 250, :b "רמ״ח איברים", :b-value 511, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:13:02.574955608Z", :model "glm-5.2"}